ap/media/learning/magic-carpet-wizard-astra.webp","alt","A carpet rider flies over a curved city toward a glowing ring.","https://threapchills.github.io/MagicCarpetWizard/","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","GameMap browser capture","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)","items",[80],"Other / unspecified agent","links","Related resources",[86],"resourceIds","section",{"_57":87,"_25":88},"Three.js","/resources/threejs/","Creator evidence",[92],"evidence",{"_57":93,"_25":94,"_95":96},"See the creator’s Astra attribution","https://github.com/threapchills/MagicCarpetWizard","note","The author-controlled repository description names GPT-6 Astra. It does not establish which coding-agent client was used or publish the initial session.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[101],{"_57":102,"_25":94,"_95":103},"Open the complete carpet-flight project","Flight, enemies, spells, procedural world, audio, races and tests. Node.js 22; npm ci then npm run dev. No API keys; optional Google Fonts fall back to system fonts.","Access type","playable","demo","Play or run",[109],{"_57":110,"_25":68,"_95":111},"Play Magic Carpet Wizard","Desktop WebGL2, mouse and keyboard. Enter starts; WASD steers/climbs, mouse plus left click aims/casts, 1–3 changes spells, Space rolls, Shift boosts, and R retries.","Game platform","Browser","Guide format","disclosure","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[119],{"_57":120,"_25":94,"_95":-7},"Read the creator’s implementation guide","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[125,126,127,128],"Play an adventure run and test flight and spells.","Read the creator’s attribution and audio notes.","Inspect flight rules, collision and rendering modules.","Adjust one obstacle or spell and test a retry and ghost race.","AI workflow / foundation context","The creator’s repository About section attributes the game to GPT-6 Astra. The README documents original procedural geometry and textures plus supplied audio; it does not publish prompts, a transcript or an exact division of human and model work.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","category","provenance","Track","3D","track","metadata","Engine","Three.js · JavaScript","engine","lead","3d","ai-assisted",[125,126,127,128],{"_57":120,"_25":94,"_17":115},{"_57":110,"_25":68,"_17":105,"_95":111},{"_57":102,"_25":94,"_154":155,"_95":103},{"_57":93,"_25":94,"_95":96},[153],"threejs","scope","complete-project",{"_157":158},"documents",{"_159":160,"_161":162},"en",[164,168,169,170,167,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,197,198,199,200,201,202,166,203,165,204,205,206,207,208,209,210,211,212,213,214,215,216,217,218,219,220,221,222,223,224],"zh",[163,164,165,166,167],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies","native-operation-details","production-debugging-contracts","production-coverage-gaps","generative-tools-research","generative-api-boundaries","generation-delivery-contracts","asset-validation-contracts","asset-selection-feedback","visual-evidence-research","visual-feedback-mechanisms","game-development-evaluation","benchmark-reproducibility","gameplay-state-contracts","agent-interface-evidence","catalog-review-coverage","source-revision-notes","community-case-research","overview","catalog","contributing","media-sources","icon-sources","content-model","skills/level-design/SKILL","skills/level-design/LICENSE","design/design-system","design/v2/design-system","editorial-art-prompts","skills/level-design/references/blockout-metrics","skills/level-design/references/case-studies","